## Deploy

- Command(s): {{DEPLOY_CMD}}
- Who: the **Principal** (or explicit per-issue delegation). Agents propose, never deploy.
- After a deploy, QA/Ops runs the post-deploy watch (below).

## Rollback (forward-only mindset)

- Immediate: {{ROLLBACK_STEP}} <!-- e.g. Cloud Run: route traffic to previous revision <name> -->
- A code rollback does **not** revert a database migration. Production recovery from a bad
  migration is a **new forward migration**, not a downgrade.

## Migration safety (design authority: your ADR)

- **Additive** (`CREATE TABLE`, nullable/defaulted `ADD COLUMN`, widening, idempotent
  reference-data upserts): rides the normal deploy path; no Action Card.
- **Destructive** (`DROP`, `RENAME`, type-narrowing, `SET NOT NULL` without default,
  validated constraints, whole-table backfills): a **hard stop for every agent**. Post the
  destructive-migration Action Card and wait for the Principal. Never couple a destructive
  migration with a code deploy. Ambiguous ⇒ destructive.

## Proposed Action Card (Gate 2)

```
## Proposed Action Card — Gate 2
Action:     <merge PR #N to main · deploy {{DEPLOY_TARGET}} · run migration>
Risk:       low|medium|high + one-line rationale
Evidence:   test summary line · eval pass rate · security verdict · CI links
Migrations: none | additive | DESTRUCTIVE (details + backup/rollback plan)
Rollback:   {{ROLLBACK_STEP}}
Awaiting:   Principal approval
```

## Post-deploy monitoring

- First 30 minutes: {{MONITOR_CMD}} <!-- log/error-rate query for the deploy target -->
- Incident: triage severity; if the deploy caused it, propose rollback (Action Card) and
  file a bug → `stage:intake` with telemetry attached. Escalate the highest severity to the
  Principal immediately.
